        "id": 216091,
        "name": "Julia",
        "username": "Julia",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/2bfe46/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-05-04T13:51:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I once upon a time (years ago, after making my Lego SotM minifigs) converted all known sizes of the (human-shaped) Multiverse characters down to 1:6th scale to make Barbies/Action Men/whatever-your-articulated, redressable-figure-of-your-choice is custom characters, and then created a spreadsheet of closest available bodys and existing doll facemolds for each of the characters (back then there were a lot fewer, obvisiously).&nbsp;</p><p>I still have the speadsheet and a lot of the heads, body parts, clothes and accessories, but after I was utterly unable to obtain this one particular head for the Unity doll (unfortunately, that head was only created for one specific doll in one particular line and never reused), I kinda lost my buzz.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Mind you, I would never have bothered with a full Guise action figure. A Guise PEZ dispenser would have done the trick.&nbsp;</p>",
